# R39 Phase 2e per-shape SHAPE-PARSE fixture (Core #12 axis coverage) —
# cell: KEYWORD `in` terminator × for-loop bare-tuple bindings
# (parser.gg parse_for_stmt).  Rust gg REJECTS `for a, b, in xs:` at
# parse (`expected pattern, found 'in'`), so this fixture cannot
# meaningfully test the trailing-comma cell against Rust.  The SH's
# post-migration `while check_tok(TOK_COMMA): advance; if check_kw(KW_IN):
# break; ...` shape ACCEPTS the trailing comma at this site
# (owner-directive 2026-08-09) — verified end-to-end via
# `sh_bootstrap_stage2_double_free_after_fmt_sweep`.
#
# What this fixture LOCKS: the non-trailing `for a, b in xs:`
# bare-tuple bindings shape parses+runs correctly on Rust gg (and,
# through the wrapper, on SH too).
void main():
    Vector[(int, int)] pairs = [(1, 10), (2, 20), (3, 30)]
    int sum = 0
    for a, b in pairs:
        sum = sum + a + b
    print(f"sum={sum}")
